{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Backtest artifact (AC 6) — planning-corpus check PASS\n\n`python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --check-planning-corpus` re-derives the pinned planning corpus and asserts exact set equality; it exited 0:\n\n- corpus rule: subject-prefix bug-fix commits, ancestors of `25fa6107f36f` (PLANNING_CORPUS_BOUNDARY)\n- corpus size: 113 (expected 113)\n- flagged (> 150 non-test lines): 13 — exactly the ADJUDICATED_SUBSTANTIVE set; missed=[]; mechanical_fp=[]\n\nFlagged set (commit, non-test lines, ticket):\n\n```\n3aec0ae90abb    183  c2ba-98bf-ca2d-481a\n08b47eb78e14    194  7c26-4ac8-04a3-440e\n5ef138d26e81    226  304e-9c0f-2068-4d0e\n96a0d5c3f2fa    180  747f-d1ba-dd43-43f4\n262616961cb4    180  30a2-4f2a-dd5a-45a0\n74051ade15c3    173  1630-0279-85ba-4e15\n517e0470ab01    225  7e77-cbe5-5bcf-4096\n992b0656d40e    162  4e21-d1a9-622b-4d4f\n0fdb9fc6cbee    640  5e40-0fe4-a966-425e\nd5733dbc97d7    419  5e40-0fe4-a966-425e\n27e1165cdbbc    264  88eb-2beb-65f5-4bc0\ne6f3283a0d0a    205  4b59-3bf9-d4a4-4768\n485873652981    230  4c1c-8588-5a3b-498b\n```\n\nCorpus-rule note: the planning analysis measured SUBJECT-PREFIX bug-fix commits (113). The shipped gate resolves trailers too; over the same range that wider rule sees 245 bug-fix commits / 24 flagged — the extra flagged members are outside the hand-adjudicated corpus, so the AC's set-equality check runs under the planning rule (encoded in --check-planning-corpus). Against today's origin/main the default gate-rule run reports 300 bug-fix commits / 33 flagged (post-planning growth; not part of the adjudicated corpus)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785789096773791001,"uuid":"0fb6385b-